.github/releases/v2.0.9.md:18:- Windows overlay z-order re-asserted after showInactive() to prevent DWM silently demoting the overlay
PERF_AUDIT.md:13:The flow is mostly correct in shape — the heavy audio work is deferred behind a `setTimeout(0)` so the IPC response returns instantly and the UI flips to overlay mode. The actual stalls come from what happens in (and around) that deferred IIFE.
PERF_AUDIT.md:46:### 1.5 Two synchronous IPC sends to non-overlay windows — **P2**
PERF_AUDIT.md:47:main.ts:1711–1712 sends `'session-reset'` to both overlay AND launcher webContents. Launcher is not active during a meeting; the message is a no-op there but still incurs structured-clone serialization cost. Minor (~0.1 ms) but multiplied across every IPC fan-out pattern in this file (see §2.3).
PERF_AUDIT.md:83:Each `webContents.send` is a structured-clone over IPC. Most of these windows don't subscribe. On a single-window setup the cost is negligible; on multi-window (overlay + launcher + settings + meeting-details) you fan a single change into 4–5 serializations.
